{"step_index":530,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T18:27:32Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T20:27:32+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T20:27:32+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/verify_proofs.py`\nTotal Lines: 120\nTotal Bytes: 4985\nShowing lines 1 to 60\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: #!/usr/bin/env python3\n2: \"\"\"tools/verify_proofs.py — authoritative, independent re-verification of every\n3: proof the prover shim persisted to results/verified_proofs/.\n4: \n5: Why this exists (run 53863): the live reprove count is gated by the HTTP client\n6: (LocalEndpointProver), whose timeout (prover_timeout_s + 30) can be SHORTER than a\n7: multi-round agentic proof, so a genuinely kernel-verified proof gets dropped from\n8: the job-level tally even though it passed. The shim now persists each verified\n9: proof the instant it passes; this script re-checks those saved artifacts with the\n10: SAME sound bare-`lean` + LEAN_PATH kernel check (LeanSubprocessProver._run_lean,\n11: canary-tested true/false), decoupling the trustworthy count from the orchestration.\n12: \n13: This is the number to cite: a proof counts iff its self-contained `.lean` file\n14: (mathlib + GraphInvariants preamble + the proof) elaborates cleanly here, with no\n15: network, no model, and no client in the loop.\n16: \n17: Usage:\n18:     .venv/bin/python tools/verify_proofs.py [--dir results/verified_proofs]\n19: Exit code is the number of proofs that FAILED re-verification (0 = all good).\n20: \"\"\"\n21: import argparse\n22: import glob\n23: import os\n24: import sys\n25: \n26: sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))))\n27: \n28: from config import CONFIG\n29: from